Source: Samsung S5E9945 vendor kernel (android14-6.1, 6.1.138 source tree),
copied without modification:
- net/ipv6/netfilter/ip6table_nat.c  (CONFIG_IP6_NF_NAT is not set on the
  device; the unified MASQUERADE target is built in)
- drivers/net/macvlan.c              (CONFIG_MACVLAN is not set)

Both import only exported KMI symbols and no core kernel code is
conditional on these options. Droidspaces probes them for its "IPv6 NAT
support" and "Macvlan support" checks.

Build: scripts/build-samsung.py 6.1 --module ip6table_nat|macvlan ...
macvlan is compiled with -DCONFIG_MACVLAN_MODULE=1: include/linux/if_macvlan.h
replaces macvlan_dev_real_dev() with BUG() when the option is off, and a
first build without the define hit it on the device (kernel BUG at
if_macvlan.h:82 in macvlan_get_link_net, from rtnl_fill_link_netnsid, when
`droidspaces check` probed macvlan). The rebuilt module contains no BUG
site.

Device (SM-S921N, 6.1.162-android14-11; macvlan sha256 3a9a56c30b3d0d92...):
with both modules loaded, `droidspaces check` (v7.2.0) reports Macvlan
support and IPv6 NAT support as present and completes without a fault.

drivers/net/ipvlan/{ipvlan.h,ipvlan_core.c,ipvlan_main.c} (CONFIG_IPVLAN is
not set), copied without modification into src/net61/ipvlan. ipvlan_l3s.c is
left out: L3S needs CONFIG_NET_L3_MASTER_DEV, a bool the device kernel was
built without, so the module offers the l2 and l3 modes and the vendor
header's own stubs refuse l3s. All 98 imports are in the vendor
Module.symvers. Build: scripts/build-samsung.py 6.1 --module ipvlan ...
